--- !u!114 &8581758879321300011
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7117142509165700568}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\n\u201CWhat he was like? People keep asking me what he was like. As if
    that\u2019s difficult, you don\u2019t have to ask me for that. Ah, Askim\u2026
    He always woke up earlier than he needed to. Said food tastes better when you
    make it before the world gets loud. I used to complain about the smell of oil
    in his clothes. Now I miss it. The stand wasn\u2019t just work. It kept us afloat.
    It was\u2026 how he stayed visible. Everyone knew where to find him. *They* keep
    asking questions. Not about the day itself. About him. What kind of people came
    by. What he talked about. As if kindness could be suspicious. As if the problem
    started at our counter.\r\n\r\nIf you\u2019re taking care of the grave, don\u2019t
    make it grand. He never liked things that tried too hard. He liked simple things.
    Warm food. A clean counter. Knowing someone would be fed before school let out\u2026
    That\u2019s enough.\u201D\r\n\r\n\n\u201CPeople think grief is loud. It isn\u2019t.
    It\u2019s waking up and realizing you don\u2019t know what to do with the morning
    anymore.\u201D\r\n\r\n\r\nDaughter \n\u201CYou\u2019re that cleaner from yesterday,
    yes? Anne told me. Thank you for this, he\u2026 I know he\u2019d be grateful
    too. Reminds me of how he always used to pack extra napkins. I also always told
    him we didn\u2019t need them. \u2018Someone always does\u2019, he\u2019d say,
    you know? I didn\u2019t like standing near the stand after school. Convenient
    for the food. For me. For the others. Everyone knew me if they knew him. Now
    I keep wishing I stayed longer.\u201D\n\nWitness\n\u201CI was there earlier.
    Not when it happened - Before. Two people came by. Didn\u2019t buy anything.
    Just stood too close. I remember thinking they were waiting for someone else.
    I keep wondering what would\u2019ve happened if I\u2019d stayed.\u201D\r\n\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
